See that big town?
One day we're gonna own that town.

18
00:02:56.681 --> 00:02:58.359
You and me.

19
00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.199
What do you think of that?

20
00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:03.960
Smart kid.

21
00:04:01.681 --> 00:04:04.199
Next stop. Martin Boulevard.

22
00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.319
Hey!

23
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.999
Uncle Pat. you'd better be careful

24
00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.319
or you're gonna
throw that back out again.

25
00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.519
Don't worry. I can handle it.
So. home from the wars. huh?

26
00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:28.560
- How you doin'?
- Oh. I'm doin' fine.

27
00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.119
Servicing all the widows
in the neighborhood now.

28
00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.719
Same ol' Uncle Pat.

29
00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.319
Flat beer from rusty pipes.

30
00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.599
If you only knew how I missed it.

31
00:04:39.681 --> 00:04:42.479
You might have changed a lot. but they
sure didn't beat the wise guy out of you.

32
00:04:42.561 --> 00:04:43.800
Not a chance of that.

33
00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.279
I saved the apartment for you.

34
00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:48.119
I sublet it to a couple of yuppies.
They loved your mother's furniture.

35
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.240
They said it was quaint.

36
00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:53.240
I still remember the day
they came to repossess it.

37
00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.000
So what are you going to do now?

38
00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.359
Make a million.

39
00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.759
In the meantime.
I'll ask McDougal to give you a job.

40
00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.439
No way!

41
00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:06.919
It was good enough for your old man.

42
00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:08.959
So was arthritis.

43
00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.919
He supported a family.
just like you're gonna have to do.

44
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.239
No. not me.
I'm not falling into that trap.

45
00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:18.119
Every man wakes up one fine morning
with the wife and kids.

46
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.839
Where'd they come from?
They weren't there last time I looked.

47
00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.160
That's 'cause most things in life.
good and bad.

48
00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.039
just kind of happen to you.

49
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.879
I'm gonna make things happen for me.

50
00:05:28.081 --> 00:05:29.679
Sure you will.

51
00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:30.960
That'll be a buck for the beer.

52
00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:38.999
What? Your nephew comes home
from serving his country

53
00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.039
and he doesn't even rate
a beer on the house?

54
00:05:41.121 --> 00:05:42.760
You don't get rich
giving things away.

55
00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.159
How do you get rich?

56
00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.479
I'm gonna give you your first lesson.
On the house.

57
00:05:47.561 --> 00:05:50.720
I've been here 25 years.
never bought a drink.

58
00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.159
Right. Eddie?

59
00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.519
I can testify to that!

60
00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.239
In 1969. the Mets won the World Series.

61
00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:01.479
Eddie here starts pounding on the bar.
demanding a round on the house.

62
00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:02.999
Drinks for everybody. he says.

63
00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.039
Tell him what I did.

64
00:06:05.121 --> 00:06:07.079
He whacked me with a club.

65
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:09.519
Almost knocked the eye out of my head.

66
00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.759
That's your way of making money?

67
00:06:11.281 --> 00:06:14.160
Outwork. outthink.
outscheme and outmaneuver.

68
00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.559
You make no friends.
Trust nobody.

69
00:06:16.641 --> 00:06:18.759
You make damn sure
you're the smartest guy in the room

70
00:06:18.841 --> 00:06:21.279
whenever the subject of money
comes up.

71
00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.919
I don't know. Uncle Pat...

72
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.960
It doesn't sound like
too much fun to me.

73
00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.799
Fun? You want fun.
go play at the beach.

74
00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.799
I think I'll try the city first.

75
00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:34.119
Here. This'll get you there in style.

76
00:06:34.201 --> 00:06:37.760
Ooh! $10. Uncle Pat.

77
00:06:38.721 --> 00:06:40.439
Why don't you buy Eddie
a binge on me. huh?

78
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.279
Eddie. you gotta be quicker than that.

79
00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.959
I've always wanted to
work on Wall Street.

80
00:07:12.041 --> 00:07:13.919
I read the Journal.
I know what's going on.

81
00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.079
I'll do whatever it takes to succeed.

82
00:07:16.161 --> 00:07:17.520
I appreciate that. Flanagan.

83
00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.759
but all our professionals
have college degrees.

84
00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:20.919
I catch on pretty quick.

85
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.679
You're wasting your time.

86
00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:23.799
We're not interested.

87
00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.960
- A guy like you. advertising.
- I have a feel for advertising.

88
00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.359
I can look at an ad
and tell you what's wrong with it.

89
00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:35.119
- We need solid credentials.
- A marketing degree is a prerequisite.

90
00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.199
Try the networks.

91
00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.959
In the Army. I spent a lot of time in
communications. I think I can help you.

92
00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.359
We need somebody
who can hit the ground running.

93
00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.679
Maybe in six or eight months. but...

94
00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:45.399
You should pursue other avenues.

95
00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.679
Maybe you should reenlist.

96
00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:49.959
I believe in positive thinking.
Never quit. Never say die.

97
00:07:50.041 --> 00:07:51.479
I want to be part of a team.

98
00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:52.999
So. what do you think?

99
00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.999
Your resume's completely inadequate.

100
00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.479
I'm willing to start at the bottom.

101
00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.799
- You're aiming too high.
- I'll do anything.

102
00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:01.519
You don't have experience.

103
00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:02.879
I need a job.

104
00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.079
We value education.

105
00:08:04.161 --> 00:08:06.519
- We require a degree.
- You should go to college.

106
00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:39.839
Bar's closed. pal.

107
00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:41.919
I'm looking for the manager.

108
00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:44.079
What's the matter?

109
00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.599
Find a hair in your quiche?

110
00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:49.439
No. I'm looking for a job.

111
00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:53.439
I see. you want to put a hair
in somebody else's quiche.

112
00:08:53.521 --> 00:08:55.519
- Did you get canned?
- I'm looking.

113
00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.879
Looking for something better.

114
00:08:58.760 --> 00:08:59.799
Coughlin's law.

115
00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.400
Anything else is
always something better.

116
00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:04.999
Coughlin's law?

117
00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:08.079
Douglas Coughlin. logical negativist.

118
00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.800
Flourished at the end of
the 20th century.

119
00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.680
Propounded a set of laws
that the world generally ignored...

120
00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:16.399
to its detriment. me.

121
00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.040
Ever work behind a bar?

122
00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.439
My uncle's in the business.

123
00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:24.120
Know how to make a Red-eye. Mr...?

124
00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:28.399
Brian Flanagan.
No. I haven't had the pleasure as yet.

125
00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:31.319
How about a Vodka Martini
with a Pernod float?

126
00:09:31.921 --> 00:09:33.519
I'm a fast learner.

127
00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.159
Could you throw a 400-pound
psychopath out the bar?

128
00:09:38.241 --> 00:09:40.199
I guess I could if I had to.

129
00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:43.479
What about a 100-pound ballerina
that's been speeding for three days?

130
00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.040
Open the door and let her pirouette out?

131
00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.720
These are just some of the tasks
you'll be asked to perform.

132
00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:54.119
This is the Upper East Side.
saloon capital of the world.

133
00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:57.319
You're ready for the big time.
young Mr. Flanagan.

134
00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:01.439
I think I can handle it.

135
00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.480
Get your act together!

136
00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:07.879
Vodka and Rose's. please.

137
00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.879
I got four people waiting for me.

138
00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.639
I'm not going back there
with three drinks.

139
00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:12.839
I'm coming.

140
00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:13.919
Absolut on the rocks.

141
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.399
Gilbey's and tonic
and a Velvet Hammer.

142
00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:19.439
- This isn't what I ordered!
- A Molson and a Cuba Libre.

143
00:10:19.521 --> 00:10:22.039
- What was that?
- A Molson and a Cuba Libre.

144
00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:24.479
And I don't want it in spurts.

145
00:10:25.281 --> 00:10:27.399
What is this?
Hire the handicapped week?

146
00:10:27.481 --> 00:10:30.360
If you're gonna sit in the water.
go to Coney Island.

147
00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:33.039
You want me to bite the top off this?

148
00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.359
This has got recipes.

149
00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.439
Ordering a Cuba Libre!

150
00:10:36.521 --> 00:10:37.999
Can I please
have a glass of water?

151
00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:39.319
He doesn't know how to make it.

152
00:10:39.401 --> 00:10:40.879
Where's my Jim Beam on the rocks?

153
00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:44.880
- It's coming. In a minute.
- I'm not leaving till I get my Cuba Libre.

154
00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:48.639
- Can I have an Orgasm?
- This isn't what I ordered.

155
00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.159
A white wine.

156
00:10:50.241 --> 00:10:51.799
You bitch!

157
00:10:51.881 --> 00:10:54.279
Why didn't you just tell me
it was a rum and coke?

158
00:10:54.361 --> 00:10:55.639
Can I have what I ordered?

159
00:10:55.721 --> 00:10:57.039
- A Bloody Mary.
- An Angel Tit.

160
00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.200
A white wine.

161
00:10:58.280 --> 00:10:59.560
Pink Squirrel.

162
00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.119
- A Friar Tuck.
- A Ding-A-Ling.

163
00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:02.799
A white wine.

164
00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:04.360
- Pink Squirrel.
- Angel Tit.

165
00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.879
- Dirty Mother.
- Can I have what I ordered?

166
00:11:06.961 --> 00:11:10.479
All right! All right!
What was it that you ordered?

167
00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:11.919
A Martini.

168
00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:13.759
What's in that?

169
00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:30.119
You get 10 percent from the waitresses.

170
00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:31.240
I don't deserve it.

171
00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:34.999
Hey. schmuck. You get money
from girls every day?

172
00:11:35.081 --> 00:11:37.079
Listen. I'm sorry I called you a bitch.

173
00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:39.399
Why? I am a bitch.

174
00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:43.759
Got yourself a new disciple?

175
00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.519
Good night. my beautiful.

176
00:11:46.201 --> 00:11:48.439
Hey. frogman.

177
00:11:48.521 --> 00:11:51.359
Anyone who can get money out of her
is a major talent.

178
00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:54.079
Come back next Thursday.
I've got five shifts open.

179
00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.119
You're offering me a job?

180
00:11:58.080 --> 00:11:59.519
The waitresses hate me.

181
00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:04.560
Wait till you've given them crabs.

182
00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:06.760
Then you'll really know hatred.

183
00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:24.440
I'd like to discuss

184
00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:26.360
the demand for money
by focusing on...

185
00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:27.679
the money multiplier.

186
00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:31.559
Add increases in currency.
deposits. reserves and bank credits.

187
00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:33.519
Then we have the sum of
an infinite series.

188
00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.039
Adding these components together.

189
00:12:36.121 --> 00:12:39.479
we find that they add up
to one plus CU over CU plus RE.

190
00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:42.039
That. simply stated.
is the money multiplier.

191
00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:43.520
Now. moving on...

192
00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.359
The essential technique of bartending.

193
00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:48.440
Less is more.

194
00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.199
The less you pour. the more you score.

195
00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:52.719
The boss does better. we do better.

196
00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:53.800
And the customer?

197
00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:55.919
Think of a customer
as a hurdler thinks of a hurdle.

198
00:12:56.001 --> 00:12:57.360
A means to an end.

199
00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:01.159
We dazzle him with ice work.
We baffle him with bottle work.

200
00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.919
There are many ways to
fool a customer.

201
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.880
The short pour.

202
00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.719
The long pour.

203
00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.279
The ice mountain. The spring thaw.

204
00:13:11.361 --> 00:13:13.560
The speed rack shuffle. The hot shot.

205
00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.839
You will learn them all.

206
00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.800
Yes. Obi-Wan.

207
00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:19.759
Both hands. Ladies. come on.

208
00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:22.799
Okay. ready?
One. two. three. Let go!

209
00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:28.479
What does it mean?

210
00:13:28.641 --> 00:13:30.879
What does it mean? Nothing!

211
00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.799
Nothing?

212
00:13:32.881 --> 00:13:34.719
All right! Nothing!

213
00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.679
Very sophisticated. man.

214
00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:42.999
- Good joke.
- You're crazy.

215
00:13:49.081 --> 00:13:50.879
You got talent.

216
00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.440
Let's go with the drinks.
We're making money tonight.

217
00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:59.559
Let's make
some money for a change.

218
00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.799
Ice!

219
00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.079
- Catch!
- Thank you.

220
00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.959
I guess that's what you learned
in college. right?

221
00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:23.080
What buns! See?

222
00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:25.159
Don't forget my beers. Bri.

223
00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:29.919
Missed me!

224
00:14:32.001 --> 00:14:33.519
The name of the game is woman.

225
00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.639
The little darlings come in here panting.

226
00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.359
Their hearts are pitter-pattering

227
00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.159
for the handsome.
all-knowing bartender.

228
00:14:40.641 --> 00:14:42.039
And in their wake.

229
00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:43.559
a parade of slobbering geeks.

230
00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:47.080
with one hand on their crotches
and the other hand on their wallets.

231
00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.759
You get the women.
and you get the bucks.

232
00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:51.200
Boy. oh. boy. you've got them.

233
00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.159
Buttons were popping.
skirts were rising.

234
00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:56.759
When you can see the color of their
panties. you know you've got talent.

235
00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.719
Stick with me. son.
I'll make you a star.

236
00:15:00.801 --> 00:15:02.479
Thanks. man.
but I gotta be honest.

237
00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.600
this is just a part-time gig for me.

238
00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:08.399
I'm in a business program.
city college. days.

239
00:15:08.481 --> 00:15:10.719
A seeker of wisdom and truth.

240
00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:15.480
This is the best work study program
you can find.

241
00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.319
To a future leader of America...

242
00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:19.639
I'll stick with the brew.

243
00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.999
Beer is for breakfast around here.

244
00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.840
Drink or be gone.

245
00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:36.399
I realize I've got a class
of budding capitalists here.

246
00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:40.799
That most of you are seeking
the fast track. lovely term.

247
00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:45.839
to a career in investment banking
or some other socially useful pursuit.

248
00:15:45.921 --> 00:15:50.959
Nevertheless. certain antiquated skills
such as reading and writing.

249
00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.399
remain a part of the curriculum.

250
00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:56.519
So. for your first assignment.

251
00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.680
I'd like you
to write your own obituaries.

252
00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.559
Not that I wish you were dead.

253
00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.399
At least. not yet. anyway.

254
00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:05.919
