At least you could apologize.

1021
01:05:26.280 --> 01:05:28.039
Apologize?

1022
01:05:28.560 --> 01:05:31.520
- Yes.
- We have to talk about this seriously.

1023
01:05:34.121 --> 01:05:37.479
Talk is overrated as a means
of resolving disputes.

1024
01:05:42.481 --> 01:05:44.960
I moved my stuff out of your place
this afternoon.

1025
01:05:45.800 --> 01:05:47.639
Left a can of Spam
in the refrigerator.

1026
01:05:47.720 --> 01:05:49.639
I hope your Brewer's yeast
doesn't take it personally.

1027
01:05:50.240 --> 01:05:51.919
Bastard!

1028
01:05:53.240 --> 01:05:54.879
Shit!

1029
01:05:55.480 --> 01:05:57.279
Oh. God. I'm sorry.

1030
01:05:59.560 --> 01:06:01.319
I'm... Brian.

1031
01:06:01.400 --> 01:06:02.959
Listen. baby.

1032
01:06:03.040 --> 01:06:04.560
I've got some interviews
set up for tomorrow.

1033
01:06:04.640 --> 01:06:06.159
Forget it!

1034
01:06:06.240 --> 01:06:08.079
I am not a salesman.

1035
01:06:08.560 --> 01:06:12.120
I tried to sell out to you.
but I couldn't close the deal.

1036
01:06:12.200 --> 01:06:13.599
Please.

1037
01:06:14.120 --> 01:06:15.879
I don't want to end it this way.

1038
01:06:15.961 --> 01:06:19.719
Jesus. everything ends badly.
otherwise it wouldn't end.

1039
01:06:20.520 --> 01:06:21.519
Believe me.

1040
01:06:21.600 --> 01:06:24.759
You'll wake up in the
morning with a sigh of relief

1041
01:06:24.840 --> 01:06:26.479
because I'm not there.

1042
01:07:05.520 --> 01:07:07.999
- Waitress.
- I'll be there in a second.

1043
01:07:12.041 --> 01:07:15.439
Excuse me. could you tell me
what the specials are please?

1044
01:07:15.520 --> 01:07:16.959
What are you doing here?

1045
01:07:17.760 --> 01:07:19.639
Bet you thought
you'd never see me again.

1046
01:07:20.160 --> 01:07:21.479
Hoped is a better word.

1047
01:07:21.560 --> 01:07:23.840
- Excuse me.
- I'll be there in a minute.

1048
01:07:24.320 --> 01:07:26.079
Miss. we have theater tickets.

1049
01:07:26.400 --> 01:07:28.279
You obviously are not here to eat.

1050
01:07:28.361 --> 01:07:29.720
so I'd appreciate it if you'd leave.

1051
01:07:29.800 --> 01:07:32.639
- Miss!
- I'll be there in a minute!

1052
01:07:32.960 --> 01:07:34.599
I'm not leaving.

1053
01:07:35.000 --> 01:07:37.199
Your sexy. little smile
is not gonna work this time.

1054
01:07:39.040 --> 01:07:40.840
I'm not leaving. That's it.

1055
01:07:41.280 --> 01:07:42.519
You're not leaving?

1056
01:07:43.600 --> 01:07:45.519
Not until you let me apologize.

1057
01:07:47.080 --> 01:07:49.839
Did you say you'd like
to see the specials. sir?

1058
01:07:49.920 --> 01:07:51.079
I'd like to see the specials.

1059
01:07:58.520 --> 01:08:00.919
Look. we've been waiting...

1060
01:08:01.001 --> 01:08:03.519
Today's specials are
Meatloaf Mozzarella.

1061
01:08:04.880 --> 01:08:06.439
Chicken à la King.

1062
01:08:08.160 --> 01:08:11.280
May I suggest
some ketchup for your fries.

1063
01:08:14.680 --> 01:08:16.360
Fuck.

1064
01:08:21.280 --> 01:08:22.999
Shit.

1065
01:08:26.760 --> 01:08:29.999
I'd think twice about
ordering the specials if I were you.

1066
01:08:39.840 --> 01:08:42.399
Spare change for my dry cleaning?

1067
01:08:42.480 --> 01:08:44.239
Sorry. Payday's Friday.

1068
01:08:44.320 --> 01:08:46.479
You wouldn't treat a stray dog
like this.

1069
01:08:46.560 --> 01:08:48.919
A stray dog can be loyal.

1070
01:08:49.001 --> 01:08:51.320
All right. I'm a rat
and there's no hope for me.

1071
01:08:51.400 --> 01:08:54.080
But even I have a right to
defend myself.

1072
01:08:54.160 --> 01:08:56.400
or at least to explain.

1073
01:08:57.361 --> 01:08:58.559
Taxi!

1074
01:09:00.360 --> 01:09:01.959
Come on in.

1075
01:09:19.721 --> 01:09:21.999
Is this our waterfall?

1076
01:09:22.080 --> 01:09:23.239
No.

1077
01:09:23.880 --> 01:09:26.040
It's terrific.

1078
01:09:26.120 --> 01:09:29.320
Yeah. it's all right.
Name's Mooney. not Monet.

1079
01:09:32.320 --> 01:09:36.519
So. why did you humiliate me
like that in Jamaica?

1080
01:09:38.200 --> 01:09:39.719
How did I humiliate you?

1081
01:09:40.520 --> 01:09:41.999
Brian. I was there.

1082
01:09:42.081 --> 01:09:44.359
I saw you go off with that woman.

1083
01:09:45.760 --> 01:09:47.719
You're such an asshole.

1084
01:09:55.000 --> 01:09:57.079
It's not as bad as it seems.

1085
01:09:57.520 --> 01:09:59.799
Doug landed a rich chick.

1086
01:10:01.001 --> 01:10:03.439
and that night he bet me
that I couldn't do the same.

1087
01:10:03.520 --> 01:10:07.519
A rich chick? You'd go with a woman
just because she had money.

1088
01:10:07.600 --> 01:10:09.479
No. it's not the money.

1089
01:10:09.560 --> 01:10:12.999
He bet me that I wasn't
good enough to hustle her.

1090
01:10:13.520 --> 01:10:15.439
Hustle her?

1091
01:10:15.520 --> 01:10:17.119
I was worth so little to you

1092
01:10:17.200 --> 01:10:19.279
that you could just take
some stupid juvenile bet?

1093
01:10:19.360 --> 01:10:22.839
No. A guy lays down a dare.
you gotta take it.

1094
01:10:24.360 --> 01:10:27.999
Brian. how do you think I felt
seeing you go off with some woman

1095
01:10:28.080 --> 01:10:29.759
after the time we spent together?

1096
01:10:29.840 --> 01:10:32.400
Hold on.
You were pushing me down there.

1097
01:10:32.480 --> 01:10:34.880
You were coming on too strong.
too fast.

1098
01:10:35.360 --> 01:10:36.920
Oh. I was pushing you?

1099
01:10:37.000 --> 01:10:38.840
You happened to be there too.

1100
01:10:38.920 --> 01:10:42.399
I thought we had something going.
I didn't play any games with you.

1101
01:10:42.600 --> 01:10:44.239
I know.

1102
01:10:48.000 --> 01:10:49.719
I'm sorry...

1103
01:10:51.320 --> 01:10:53.120
I guess I just got spooked.

1104
01:10:54.200 --> 01:10:57.799
But now I know I can handle it.

1105
01:10:57.880 --> 01:10:59.719
Oh. you can handle it. huh?

1106
01:11:01.280 --> 01:11:03.079
What if you got spooked again?

1107
01:11:03.760 --> 01:11:05.199
I won't.

1108
01:11:05.280 --> 01:11:07.999
- I'll bet I can spook you.
- No way.

1109
01:11:09.841 --> 01:11:11.360
I'm pregnant.

1110
01:11:13.040 --> 01:11:14.559
I'm spooked.

1111
01:11:16.600 --> 01:11:18.080
It's mine?

1112
01:11:19.041 --> 01:11:23.319
- I was only asking!
- You're not going to be burdened.

1113
01:11:23.400 --> 01:11:26.279
You can still go out and make a million.
Don't worry.

1114
01:11:26.360 --> 01:11:29.720
I'm not worried.
I mean. I am worried.

1115
01:11:29.800 --> 01:11:32.399
I don't want to talk about it anymore.

1116
01:11:32.481 --> 01:11:33.919
Just go!

1117
01:11:34.200 --> 01:11:37.239
- Why?
- Because I want you to go! Just go!

1118
01:11:40.480 --> 01:11:43.359
You let me come up here just so
you could kick me out. Didn't you?

1119
01:11:56.481 --> 01:11:57.759
No.

1120
01:11:59.960 --> 01:12:01.759
No. just get out!

1121
01:12:02.600 --> 01:12:03.559
I know you're upset.

1122
01:12:03.640 --> 01:12:06.399
but if this is the way it's gonna be.
why'd you tell me about the baby?

1123
01:12:07.160 --> 01:12:10.519
Because I knew it would be
the best way to get you out of my life.

1124
01:12:34.560 --> 01:12:35.479
Madison Square Garden.

1125
01:12:35.561 --> 01:12:37.519
Syracuse trying to stay
within striking distance...

1126
01:12:40.320 --> 01:12:42.680
That's for cigarette change!

1127
01:12:42.760 --> 01:12:44.559
When you hand it to me. it's for change.

1128
01:12:44.640 --> 01:12:48.079
When you put it on the edge of the bar.
it's a tip.

1129
01:12:48.200 --> 01:12:51.239
- Hey. kid!
- Hi. Uncle Pat. Ed. How are you?

1130
01:12:52.640 --> 01:12:54.559
I got a problem.
Got time for a quick talk?

1131
01:12:54.640 --> 01:12:57.080
Make it fast. I'm real busy here.

1132
01:13:02.041 --> 01:13:03.039
What's the matter?

1133
01:13:07.360 --> 01:13:08.959
I'm going to be a father.

1134
01:13:10.720 --> 01:13:13.000
- That's it. bar's closed. Finish up.
- Come on!

1135
01:13:13.080 --> 01:13:14.679
Come on. hit the road.
Let's go.

1136
01:13:14.760 --> 01:13:17.439
- Eddie. finish up. Everybody out.
- What?

1137
01:13:19.200 --> 01:13:22.719
You ought to know better than to come
to a bartender for advice.

1138
01:13:23.440 --> 01:13:25.279
What am I going to do about this girl?

1139
01:13:25.360 --> 01:13:26.639
Nothing.

1140
01:13:27.240 --> 01:13:28.360
What do you mean. nothing?

1141
01:13:28.960 --> 01:13:30.799
She's not trying to shake you down.

1142
01:13:30.880 --> 01:13:33.239
not making you marry her.
you don't care about her.

1143
01:13:33.320 --> 01:13:34.520
You can walk away
from the whole thing.

1144
01:13:38.160 --> 01:13:39.839
What if I do care about her?

1145
01:13:40.280 --> 01:13:41.639
Then you got a problem.

1146
01:13:46.400 --> 01:13:48.800
Jordan.
I just want to talk to you.

1147
01:13:50.240 --> 01:13:53.199
She's not hiding.
She's not home.

1148
01:13:53.280 --> 01:13:55.679
She's at her parents' place.
Go bang down their door.

1149
01:13:56.000 --> 01:13:57.919
You wouldn't happen to know
where that is. would you?

1150
01:13:58.440 --> 01:14:00.440
Sure. Park Avenue. Corner of 67th.

1151
01:14:02.600 --> 01:14:05.159
- Park Avenue?
- Yeah.

1152
01:14:11.680 --> 01:14:13.359
You get here
when you say you will.

1153
01:14:13.440 --> 01:14:15.199
or you won't work in this
building again.

1154
01:14:15.280 --> 01:14:16.760
Excuse me.

1155
01:14:16.840 --> 01:14:18.319
So you'll be here what time?

1156
01:14:18.400 --> 01:14:20.079
I don't mean to bother you...

1157
01:14:20.160 --> 01:14:21.999
What time did you say you'd be here?

1158
01:14:22.080 --> 01:14:23.599
Hello?

1159
01:14:23.680 --> 01:14:25.639
Sorry. what apartment
are the Mooneys in?

1160
01:14:25.720 --> 01:14:27.799
It's a penthouse.
Your name. please?

1161
01:14:27.881 --> 01:14:30.319
- Brian Flanagan.
- Are the Mooneys expecting you?

1162
01:14:30.400 --> 01:14:31.679
No. not exactly.

1163
01:14:31.760 --> 01:14:34.880
All visitors have to be announced.
Mr. Flanagan.

1164
01:14:46.560 --> 01:14:49.119
Mr. Flanagan.
would you come in. please?

1165
01:14:49.200 --> 01:14:51.679
- May I take your coat. sir?
- Okay.

1166
01:14:55.080 --> 01:14:57.119
There'll be someone with you
in a moment.

1167
01:14:57.200 --> 01:14:58.399
Thank you.

1168
01:15:16.161 --> 01:15:17.359
I'm Richard Mooney.

1169
01:15:18.560 --> 01:15:21.279
- I'm Jordan's father.
- I'm Brian Flanagan.

1170
01:15:22.240 --> 01:15:24.399
- I've come to see her.
- She's not here.

1171
01:15:24.480 --> 01:15:26.399
But come in.

1172
01:15:26.480 --> 01:15:28.199
I'd like to talk to you.

1173
01:15:32.160 --> 01:15:33.440
Sit down.

1174
01:15:38.000 --> 01:15:41.639
I've certainly heard a lot about you
in the last couple of days.

1175
01:15:44.440 --> 01:15:47.439
I don't know what really happened
between the two of you. but...

1176
01:15:48.640 --> 01:15:51.439
I must say. you've got a lot of nerve

1177
01:15:51.520 --> 01:15:53.559
coming up here after
what you did to my daughter.

1178
01:15:53.640 --> 01:15:55.599
I understand that.

1179
01:15:55.680 --> 01:15:58.279
and I realize that Jordan
is very upset.

1180
01:15:59.361 --> 01:16:00.759
But if I could talk to her.
make her see

1181
01:16:00.840 --> 01:16:03.159
that I'm gonna
stick by her through this...

1182
01:16:03.240 --> 01:16:05.679
I hope you're not suggesting
that you'll marry her.

1183
01:16:09.720 --> 01:16:13.159
I'm not sure what we're gonna do.
We have a lot to talk about...

1184
01:16:13.240 --> 01:16:16.319
The hell you do!

1185
01:16:17.480 --> 01:16:20.439
Look. I know Jordan a lot better
than you do.

1186
01:16:20.520 --> 01:16:23.080
and I've never seen her
as unhappy as she is at this moment.

1187
01:16:23.520 --> 01:16:26.559
She is just not very wise
in the ways of the world.

1188
01:16:26.641 --> 01:16:30.159
Right now. what she needs around
are people she can trust.

1189
01:16:30.240 --> 01:16:33.240
- She can trust me.
- She doesn't want to see you.

1190
01:16:34.120 --> 01:16:35.999
She doesn't even want to talk to you.

1191
01:16:37.560 --> 01:16:40.279
Just wait here one moment.
will you please?

1192
01:16:49.961 --> 01:16:51.679
- Good afternoon. Miss Mooney.
- Hi.

1193
01:16:57.000 --> 01:17:00.399
- Mr. Mooney. I think I'm just gonna...
- Flanagan. here.

1194
01:17:01.040 --> 01:17:03.279
- What the hell's this?
- That's for you.

1195
01:17:07.320 --> 01:17:09.840
$10.000.

1196
01:17:11.040 --> 01:17:15.119
- Is that all your daughter's worth?
- How much will it take?

1197
01:17:15.481 --> 01:17:17.120
I don't want your goddamn money.

1198
01:17:18.081 --> 01:17:20.439
You can't buy me out of Jordan's life!

1199
01:17:20.760 --> 01:17:23.399
You think I'd let some bartender
destroy my daughter's life?

1200
01:17:23.480 --> 01:17:25.999
- That is her choice!
- The hell you say!

1201
01:17:26.080 --> 01:17:27.960
What is going on here?

1202
01:17:28.480 --> 01:17:30.359
Jordan. I came here to talk to you.

1203
01:17:30.440 --> 01:17:33.999
- If you don't get out of here...
- Dad. I'll handle this!

1204
01:17:35.160 --> 01:17:37.839
I know the other night
I didn't say the right things.

1205
01:17:37.920 --> 01:17:39.999
God knows I have not done
the right things.

1206
01:17:40.960 --> 01:17:43.519
But I think there's a chance for us.

1207
01:17:44.240 --> 01:17:45.839
Brian. there is no us.

1208
01:17:45.921 --> 01:17:48.399
There are too many things
about us that don't work.

1209
01:17:48.480 --> 01:17:50.239
What about the baby?

1210
01:17:50.320 --> 01:17:52.760
A kid. I mean.
our kid needs a father.

1211
01:17:54.240 --> 01:17:56.279
Not one that won't be around in a year.

1212
01:17:56.360 --> 01:17:58.999
With your lifestyle.
what kind of father would you be?

1213
01:18:00.200 --> 01:18:03.439
Jordan. I want a second chance.

1214
01:18:04.920 --> 01:18:06.119
No.

1215
01:18:06.200 --> 01:18:09.199
- I deserve a second chance.
- No.

1216
01:18:10.440 --> 01:18:13.519
How will I ever know
that you're being honest with me?

1217
01:18:13.600 --> 01:18:15.559
You can barely be honest
with yourself.

1218
01:18:15.640 --> 01:18:17.119
Honest?

1219
01:18:17.200 --> 01:18:19.039
Were you so honest?

1220
01:18:19.120 --> 01:18:21.519
Why didn't you tell me
you were the original rich chick?

1221
01:18:21.600 --> 01:18:23.799
Because you're so hung up on money.

1222
01:18:23.880 --> 01:18:27.679
I was afraid I'd never know
how you felt about me.

1223
01:18:27.760 --> 01:18:30.879
Me! How you'd really feel
about me.

1224
01:18:34.080 --> 01:18:35.399
See this?

1225
01:18:36.600 --> 01:18:40.479
This is your father's idea
of how to get me out of your life.

1226
01:18:44.320 --> 01:18:48.159
This is how hung up on money I am.

1227
01:18:49.600 --> 01:18:51.359
As for the way I feel about you.

1228
01:18:53.680 --> 01:18:55.919
I guess you'll never know.

1229
01:19:05.041 --> 01:19:06.999
Let me in!

1230
01:19:07.080 --> 01:19:08.519
Hey. what about us?

1231
01:19:08.600 --> 01:19:10.199
We've been here for two hours!

1232
01:19:10.280 --> 01:19:12.679
Let us in. Henry. It's cold out here.

1233
01:19:12.760 --> 01:19:13.839
Henry? Remember me?

1234
01:19:13.920 --> 01:19:15.759
I'm Bruce Springsteen's cousin.

1235
01:19:15.840 --> 01:19:17.679
- You look more like his couch.
- Henry!

1236
01:19:17.760 --> 01:19:19.720
I'm Doug's friend.

1237
01:19:19.800 --> 01:19:22.600
Mr. Coughlin doesn't have any friends
on a Saturday night.

1238
01:19:22.680 --> 01:19:24.959
- Good evening. Henry.
- Hey!

1239
01:19:30.800 --> 01:19:33.759
- Where's Doug Coughlin?
- Over there.

1240
01:19:34.640 --> 01:19:36.320
Hey. you!

1241
01:19:36.640 --> 01:19:37.759
Doug!

1242
01:19:38.160 --> 01:19:40.280
- Coughlin! Doug!
- Flanagan!

1243
01:19:41.040 --> 01:19:43.599
My best friend in the world!
My only friend!

1244
01:19:44.001 --> 01:19:45.439
Piss off. Henry. It's okay.

1245
01:19:45.520 --> 01:19:48.719
It's great to see you. my only friend.
Sit down.

1246
01:19:48.801 --> 01:19:51.359
It looks like you've got
a lot of friends here this evening.

1247
01:19:51.440 --> 01:19:53.119
- Proctologist's dream.
- What?

1248
01:19:53.200 --> 01:19:55.119
Wall-to-wall assholes.

1249
01:19:55.200 --> 01:19:58.839
- Great to see you. Flanagan.
- I've come to pay off my bet.

1250
01:19:58.920 --> 01:20:01.159
- Brian!
- Kerry!

1251
01:20:03.440 --> 01:20:04.840
What are you doing here?

1252
01:20:05.521 --> 01:20:07.720
I've come
to beg and plead for a job.

1253
01:20:08.001 --> 01:20:11.000
It'd be great to get some talent
behind the bar.

1254
01:20:24.000 --> 01:20:26.399
Let's go somewhere where
we can appreciate this.

1255
01:20:26.480 --> 01:20:27.880
Come on.

1256
01:20:36.000 --> 01:20:37.519
Get in there.

1257
01:20:37.600 --> 01:20:39.599
Get in there and spend some money.

1258
01:20:39.681 --> 01:20:41.759
Keep me in the manner
I'm accustomed to.

1259
01:20:41.840 --> 01:20:44.799
Get in there and spend some money.
you two.

1260
01:20:45.240 --> 01:20:47.199
What do you think of my rowing boat?

1261
01:20:48.560 --> 01:20:50.559
Jesus Christ!

1262
01:20:50.641 --> 01:20:52.079
Come aboard. ye land lubber!

1263
01:20:56.360 --> 01:20:58.200
Baccarat crystal.

1264
01:20:59.040 --> 01:21:01.279
Louis XIII. Voilà.

1265
01:21:02.400 --> 01:21:04.279
Should we let it breathe?

1266
01:21:04.361 --> 01:21:07.839
It hasn't breathed in 50 years.
It's dead.

1267
01:21:07.921 --> 01:21:09.560
Let's just drink it.

1268
01:21:21.320 --> 01:21:24.839
- Health and friendship?
- Life and love.

1269
01:21:33.560 --> 01:21:38.640
Douglas Coughlin.
your ship has certainly come in!

1270
01:21:42.000 --> 01:21:43.359
My ship.

1271
01:21:44.480 --> 01:21:48.559
My ship is going down.
and I'm going down with it.

1272
01:21:48.640 --> 01:21:50.879
- How's that?
- All this is an illusion.

1273
01:21:52.000 --> 01:21:54.840
I'm on my ass.
I haven't got a pot to piss in.

1274
01:21:56.920 --> 01:21:59.199
$100.000 a week. Painful.

1275
01:22:00.480 --> 01:22:03.880
I should've read some of
your sacred books. young Flanagan.

1276
01:22:05.121 --> 01:22:09.360
The only thing I know about saloons is
how to pour whiskey and run my mouth.

1277
01:22:09.960 --> 01:22:12.839
I knew nothing about insurance.

1278
01:22:14.520 --> 01:22:19.800
or sales tax. or the building code.
or labor costs.

1279
01:22:19.880 --> 01:22:23.279
or the power company.
or purchasing. or linens.

1280
01:22:23.361 --> 01:22:25.759
Everyone with a hand
stuck it in my pocket.

1281
01:22:25.840 --> 01:22:27.679
You must make enough to cover that.

1282
01:22:28.000 --> 01:22:32.000
If I'd stuck to what I know best.
which is almost nothing.

1283
01:22:33.400 --> 01:22:37.039
Instead I put all the cash
into commodities.

1284
01:22:37.120 --> 01:22:40.159
And blew the fucking lot.

1285
01:22:41.440 --> 01:22:45.720
On the margin.
Buy. cover. buy. cover.

1286
01:22:46.640 --> 01:22:49.119
I wanted it fast.

1287
01:22:52.161 --> 01:22:54.200
See the headlines.

1288
01:22:54.280 --> 01:22:58.959
Douglas Coughlin.
from bartender to billionaire.

1289
01:23:04.800 --> 01:23:06.399
Hey. take it easy.

1290
01:23:06.480 --> 01:23:07.520
Relax.

1291
01:23:08.520 --> 01:23:12.079
The luck is gone. the brain is shot.

1292
01:23:12.160 --> 01:23:14.640
But the liquor. we still got.

1293
01:23:18.200 --> 01:23:19.959
Doug?

1294
01:23:21.400 --> 01:23:23.359
Are you down there?

1295
01:23:23.440 --> 01:23:28.159
She knows nothing about this.
She thinks I'm a fucking hero.

1296
01:23:33.960 --> 01:23:38.319
My princess. My dream.

1297
01:23:38.400 --> 01:23:41.120
Baby. not again.

1298
01:23:41.200 --> 01:23:42.599
I want to go home.

1299
01:23:43.280 --> 01:23:44.400
Come here.

1300
01:23:45.921 --> 01:23:47.079
Toast. Flanagan.

1301
01:23:48.080 --> 01:23:51.599
To the first and last person
I ever cared about.

1302
01:23:53.601 --> 01:23:55.199
My wife.

1303
01:23:55.280 --> 01:23:56.439
Doug?

1304
01:23:57.880 --> 01:23:59.839
Doug. wake up.

1305
01:23:59.920 --> 01:24:02.079
I want to go home.

1306
01:24:22.960 --> 01:24:26.520
You know you're the only person
in the world Doug respects?

1307
01:24:28.920 --> 01:24:30.879
We were a good team once.

1308
01:24:32.681 --> 01:24:34.600
Walk me to my apartment.

1309
01:24:34.680 --> 01:24:36.959
I hate going to that place alone.

1310
01:24:40.800 --> 01:24:43.199
- I better check on Doug.
- Please?

1311
01:24:44.481 --> 01:24:46.479
I want to talk about Doug.

1312
01:24:46.560 --> 01:24:48.239
About his problems.

1313
01:25:24.400 --> 01:25:27.599
Doug says
you're incredible with women.

1314
01:25:27.681 --> 01:25:29.919
A real lady-killer.

1315
01:25:30.001 --> 01:25:31.759
Is that what he says?

1316
01:25:32.960 --> 01:25:34.839
What's your secret weapon?

1317
01:25:36.240 --> 01:25:39.679
What you see is what you get.

1318
01:25:57.760 --> 01:26:00.079
- Hold it.
- What'd you do that for?

1319
01:26:04.960 --> 01:26:08.199
I can't make it
with my best friend's old lady.

1320
01:26:10.040 --> 01:26:12.199
Am I supposed to
live with the same man.

1321
01:26:12.280 --> 01:26:14.519
day in and day out. forever.

1322
01:26:14.600 --> 01:26:16.439
and have no one else in my life?

1323
01:26:16.520 --> 01:26:18.919
Yes. It's called marriage.

1324
01:26:19.000 --> 01:26:20.959
You wanted this as much as I did.

1325
01:26:21.040 --> 01:26:22.680
That's why you're up here.

1326
01:26:22.760 --> 01:26:24.239
But you can't do it now. can you?

1327
01:26:25.200 --> 01:26:26.279
You're scared.

1328
01:26:28.960 --> 01:26:30.799
I don't know what the fuck I'm doing.

1329
01:26:31.160 --> 01:26:32.719
You're just scared!

1330
01:26:56.200 --> 01:26:57.519
Hey. Doug!

1331
01:27:08.360 --> 01:27:12.519
Help me!
Somebody help me!

1332
01:27:14.720 --> 01:27:17.120
Somebody help me!

1333
01:27:29.080 --> 01:27:31.640
Is there anything
you can tell me about what happened?

1334
01:28:06.120 --> 01:28:08.999
The Lord is my shepherd.
I shall not want...

1335
01:28:47.800 --> 01:28:50.599
My dearest Brian.

1336
01:28:50.680 --> 01:28:52.879
a guy like me looks in the mirror.

1337
01:28:52.960 --> 01:28:55.799
He either grins
or he starts to fade away.

1338
01:28:56.480 --> 01:28:59.519
and I haven't seen anything
to grin about in a long time.

1339
01:29:01.160 --> 01:29:06.639
This may not be the most graceful exit.
but I know when the bottle's empty.

1340
01:29:06.720 --> 01:29:09.519
that the only thing
I'm really gonna miss

1341
01:29:09.600 --> 01:29:11.919
is the conversations we had going.

1342
01:29:13.440 --> 01:29:17.279
At least I get the last word.
even if I had to mail it in.

1343
01:29:18.960 --> 01:29:23.199
Coughlin's law. bury the dead.
they stink up the joint.

1344
01:29:23.760 --> 01:29:26.319
The rest of Coughlin's Laws. ignore.

1345
01:29:26.760 --> 01:29:28.959
The guy was always full of shit.

1346
01:29:32.520 --> 01:29:34.959
But I guess you knew that already.

1347
01:29:58.720 --> 01:30:01.239
- Mooney's apartment. Brian...
- I know who you are.

1348
01:30:01.320 --> 01:30:03.439
I've been instructed
not to let you in here.

1349
01:30:03.520 --> 01:30:05.279
- If you'll just call...
- Leave now!

1350
01:30:06.081 --> 01:30:08.719
I just want to
talk to her for a few minutes.

1351
01:30:08.800 --> 01:30:10.159
I don't want to cause any trouble.

1352
01:30:10.240 --> 01:30:13.200
- Send her a letter. Out!
- Get your hands off me. man.

1353
01:30:13.280 --> 01:30:14.599
Out!

1354
01:30:17.960 --> 01:30:19.359
Hey!

1355
01:30:30.081 --> 01:30:32.759
- Where's Jordan?
- She's in there.

1356
01:30:32.840 --> 01:30:34.279
But you can't go in there!

1357
01:30:34.360 --> 01:30:35.399
Open the door!

1358
01:30:35.480 --> 01:30:37.119
Jordan?

1359
01:30:37.680 --> 01:30:39.000
Jordan!

1360
01:30:39.080 --> 01:30:40.679
- I have to talk to you.
- What's going on?

1361
01:30:40.760 --> 01:30:44.039
Please. there's so many things.
I don't know where to begin.

1362
01:30:44.120 --> 01:30:45.119
Doug is dead.

1363
01:30:45.960 --> 01:30:46.959
What?

1364
01:30:47.040 --> 01:30:49.839
- He killed himself.
- Brian!

1365
01:30:49.920 --> 01:30:52.639
He was my best friend.
but he was too proud to let me help him.

1366
01:30:52.720 --> 01:30:55.639
He was too proud to show
how he felt until it was too late.

1367
01:30:55.721 --> 01:30:57.399
I don't want to make
that same mistake.

1368
01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:01.239
He pushed right past me
into the sitting room...

1369
01:31:01.320 --> 01:31:03.839
I thought I told you to keep
that punk out of this house!

1370
01:31:03.920 --> 01:31:05.880
- He got by me.
- Jordan. are you in there?

1371
01:31:06.200 --> 01:31:09.679
I have saved money. I've worked out
a loan with my uncle for some more.

1372
01:31:09.760 --> 01:31:13.079
With hard work. I know I can turn it
into something great.

1373
01:31:13.160 --> 01:31:16.840
Brian. I know you can.
but it doesn't really matter.

1374
01:31:16.920 --> 01:31:17.919
Listen to me!

1375
01:31:18.000 --> 01:31:20.120
Get me the key!

1376
01:31:20.600 --> 01:31:22.119
I love you! I want to marry you.

1377
01:31:22.640 --> 01:31:24.959
I've loved you from the first moment
I saw you. Jordan.

1378
01:31:25.320 --> 01:31:27.960
Please. come with me.

1379
01:31:28.960 --> 01:31:31.599
Flanagan.
get the hell out of my house!

1380
01:31:31.680 --> 01:31:34.039
Jordan. wake up! Don't you see
why he's come back here?

1381
01:31:34.121 --> 01:31:37.079
- He's only come back for one reason. for the money.
- That's not true. I don't want a thing from you!

1382
01:31:37.160 --> 01:31:39.759
You're not going to get one penny.
He's a loser!

1383
01:31:39.840 --> 01:31:41.959
I'm not a loser.
Please. Jordan. come with me.

1384
01:31:42.040 --> 01:31:44.719
- Get him out of here.
- Stay out of this.

1385
01:31:44.800 --> 01:31:47.119
- Please.
- Throw this bum out of here!

1386
01:31:47.720 --> 01:31:48.759
Hold it!

1387
01:31:49.201 --> 01:31:50.559
Jordan. don't go!

1388
01:31:50.640 --> 01:31:53.439
If you walk out of this house.
don't bother coming back.

1389
01:31:53.601 --> 01:31:56.480
- I love him. and I'm going!
- You're not going anywhere!

1390
01:31:56.560 --> 01:31:58.559
Jordan! Stop her!

1391
01:31:59.160 --> 01:32:00.440
- Get off of me!
- Don't fucking handle her.

1392
01:32:00.520 --> 01:32:01.839
She's pregnant!

1393
01:32:03.560 --> 01:32:05.039
You asshole!

1394
01:32:20.201 --> 01:32:22.279
It didn't have to be this way.
you know.

1395
01:32:33.160 --> 01:32:34.359
You're on your own.

1396
01:32:34.881 --> 01:32:37.239
It's the only way I want it.

1397
01:32:43.600 --> 01:32:46.759
A toast!
To the bride. and to my nephew!

1398
01:32:46.840 --> 01:32:49.519
- All the happiness!
- Salute!

1399
01:32:51.360 --> 01:32:52.719
There you go!

1400
01:32:52.800 --> 01:32:54.959
<i>I've been lied to</i>

1401
01:32:55.041 --> 01:32:58.719
<i>When will I be loved?</i>

1402
01:32:58.800 --> 01:32:59.919
Right now. baby!

1403
01:33:00.000 --> 01:33:01.519
Oh. yeah!

1404
01:33:03.320 --> 01:33:09.999
<i>I've been turned down.
I've been pushed 'round</i>

1405
01:33:10.720 --> 01:33:15.679
<i>When will I be loved?</i>

1406
01:33:20.160 --> 01:33:22.399
You realize we're both
completely insane.

1407
01:33:22.480 --> 01:33:23.840
Yes.

1408
01:33:24.480 --> 01:33:26.840
You'll probably want to divorce me
in three weeks.

1409
01:33:26.920 --> 01:33:29.759
Probably.
No. you'll want to divorce me.

1410
01:33:29.840 --> 01:33:33.119
- I'll be all fat and ugly.
- Just as long as you don't get too fat.

1411
01:33:33.880 --> 01:33:37.879
I am going to be very fat.
and you are going to love it!

1412
01:33:49.761 --> 01:33:51.439
Brian. give us a poem.

1413
01:33:51.520 --> 01:33:53.320
Yeah! Poem!

1414
01:33:53.400 --> 01:33:55.039
- Poem?
- Do one. Bri!

1415
01:33:55.120 --> 01:33:57.160
- Poem?
- Poem! Yeah!

1416
01:33:59.280 --> 01:34:01.039
- Poem?
- Poem!

1417
01:34:01.120 --> 01:34:02.640
We want a poem!

1418
01:34:02.720 --> 01:34:04.119
All right. Poem!

1419
01:34:04.200 --> 01:34:07.040
- Poem!
- All right. Brian!

1420
01:34:14.480 --> 01:34:16.599
Okay. a poem.

1421
01:34:18.320 --> 01:34:20.239
This poem is entitled

1422
01:34:21.560 --> 01:34:24.199
Flanagan's Advice to
His Unborn Child.

1423
01:34:28.960 --> 01:34:32.919
If Jordan gives birth to
a fine Irish son.

1424
01:34:33.000 --> 01:34:35.919
there'll be Cocktails & Dreams
for him one day to run.

1425
01:34:37.081 --> 01:34:40.119
A business that shall yield
a financial windfall.

1426
01:34:40.200 --> 01:34:41.959
It better!

1427
01:34:42.040 --> 01:34:43.159
Yes.

1428
01:34:43.960 --> 01:34:46.680
To be franchised in every
suburban shopping mall.

1429
01:34:46.760 --> 01:34:49.280
A dynasty!
You're founding a dynasty!

1430
01:34:50.120 --> 01:34:51.559
Now...

1431
01:34:52.800 --> 01:34:56.319
If a daughter arrives to bless
our clan.

1432
01:34:57.600 --> 01:35:00.079
I guess the shit
will certainly hit the fan.

1433
01:35:02.760 --> 01:35:06.199
But this I shall promise to thee.

1434
01:35:06.281 --> 01:35:08.880
I'll never let her marry
a guy like me.

1435
01:35:09.960 --> 01:35:16.319
Still. if our child is the naughtiest
of girls or the wildest of men.

1436
01:35:16.400 --> 01:35:19.279
I swear.
I'll be the best dad I can.

1437
01:35:19.360 --> 01:35:23.199
And never ever get spooked again.

1438
01:35:27.681 --> 01:35:29.519
I bet I can still spook you.

1439
01:35:29.601 --> 01:35:31.039
No way.

1440
01:35:37.200 --> 01:35:41.839
Twins?

1441
01:35:42.081 --> 01:35:43.040
Twins!

1442
01:35:43.120 --> 01:35:45.279
- Yeah!
- All right!

1443
01:35:45.560 --> 01:35:48.079
- Drinks are on the house!
- No!

1444
01:35:48.160 --> 01:35:50.359
Bar is open!

1445
01:35:51.305 --> 01:36:51.830
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm
